WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:05.780
 It's like playing by braille.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:10.490
You are supposed
to play by feel.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.610
I've been with music since
I was practically born.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.860
I can't live without
playing the violin.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.290
It's all about the
music that's relaxed

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:26.860
or music that's intense that
just kills you in a good way.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.710
In this class, I'm going
to talk about intonation,

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:32.680
talk about vibrato, talk
about colors, posture,

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.600
different styles of playing.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.790
Make the bow work for you.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:39.220
Don't force the bow to jump.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:44.020
The bow says, I'm only
jumping if you leave me alone.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.850
To be a musician, it's
almost like to be a magician.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.660
You don't want the listener
to realize what you're doing.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:55.420
If you get all of
that stuff you can

00:00:55.420 --> 00:01:00.070
learn to play the
violin in two hours.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:00.970
I'm just kidding.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:09.410
The old-fashioned master classes
is when the student plays

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.967
and the teacher says, let
me show you how it goes.

00:01:11.967 --> 00:01:12.800
That's not teaching.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.240
That's basically showing.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.810
I want, whenever they do
something, to be their own.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.780
When I'm playing, if I don't
feel something in the music,

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.140
nothing is going to happen.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.220
When you connect with the
music, that connection

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.290
will radiate through
the audience.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.980
I'm going to bring some
of my students to sit in

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.432
and to have a discussion.

00:01:34.432 --> 00:01:36.640
Is there a difference between
being intense and being

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.740
passionate?

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.790
If you can feel my
enthusiasm for music,

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.810
the class has
accomplished a lot.

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:46.420
To be happy,
forming great music,

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:50.020
and enjoy what you are
doing, what could be better?

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:54.085
I'm Itzhak Perlman, and
this is my MasterClass.

